## Signal-bus opt-ins

If `WIZARD_PWSH_CONTROL=1` is set and the wizard PowerShell fork is on PATH,
prefer the signal bus over OCR / polling:

- `Read-WizardSignal -Topic process.heartbeat` instead of repeated
  screenshots of a launching app.
- `Read-WizardSignal -Topic cognitive.pulse` to fetch the current pulse body
  when needed (when signal-mode pulse is enabled in Wizard_Erasmus).

## Skill triggers

Five wizard-kit skills are installed under `~/.codex/skills/`:

| Skill | Use when |
|-------|----------|
| `conversation-forensics` | mining prior Codex conversations on this PC |
| `resume-interrupted-work` | continuing a session interrupted by reboot / time gap |
| `research-to-md` | research-only deliverables, no code changes |
| `live-runtime-triage` | something running on this PC misbehaving; inspect before edit |
| `verified-delivery` | end-to-end test → focused commits → push |

Trigger only on the matching shapes described in each skill's `description`
field, not as catch-all defaults.

## Tool preferences

- `Get-AIContext`, `Find-Code`, `Find-Repos`, `Find-CodeAcrossRepos` —
  bounded ripgrep alternatives via the wizard PowerShell module.
- `Invoke-Bounded` for any subprocess whose output might exceed 16 KB or run
  longer than 120 s.
- `Read-WizardSignal` over OCR / polling.

